+# Mira head/hair candidate v60 — preserved, not adopted
+
+The user corrected the production method on 2026-09-16: generate much smaller individual parts first, then build and assemble those parts into the fixed complete design. This larger head/hair candidate is preserved as reusable material; further shape development stopped at that correction. Geometry checkpoint: `44477c14dd6dd0db3d57096f12d77680dc4d1946`. Shared assembly source, camera, gameplay, other roles and production skin defaults were not edited in this worktree.
+
+The seven fixed generated reference sheets are recorded by exact hash in `src/assets/characters/mira-head-v60-design.json`. Head FRONT, profile and BACK guide the head; the complete sheet controls proportions and garment assembly controls neck/collar ownership. These fictional design images are not a scan, metrically calibrated reconstruction or an exact likeness guarantee. Source remains the archived CC0 MakeHuman hm08 OBJ. No external asset was downloaded or reference portrait projected onto UVs.
+
+The new generator registers the original full source, applies nine smooth semantic shape controls, then performs source-aware endpoint QEM with original UV corner pairs. The 4,244 source head vertices include 3,036 moved vertices, maximum authored displacement 9.541 mm; 1,201 protected eye/mouth/neck vertices retain exact positions. Source triangle normal comparison has minimum cosine 0.94817. The final face has 2,046 triangles and 1,262 render vertices. Its source approximation maximum is 3.122 mm and p95 is 1.405 mm, measured against the **deliberately deformed full source**, not the old face or the generated artwork. A fresh 20.507-second generator replay reproduced both generated files byte for byte.
+
+The hair comprises 197 fitted source scalp triangles and 24 closed, curved, three-section clumps (480 triangles), plus 40 brow triangles. It replaces the old hair sphere and cylinder brows. Each clump is a separate closed component with positive signed volume; the combined overlapping scalp/clumps are not one watertight shell. Coarse silhouette masses remain a limitation: strand detail, material appearance and resemblance to the art have not been accepted.
+
+| Actual native CPU actor | Before | Candidate with 4 hooks | Difference |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| Visible instance triangles | 6,718 | 7,591 | +873 |
+| Visible meshes | 13 | 13 | 0 |
+| Geometry array bytes | 319,180 | 352,806 | +33,626 |
+| NPC face triangles | 1,646 | 2,046 | +400 |
+
+The clothing author's final 9,508-triangle candidate plus this +873 is **10,381 triangles by arithmetic**, not an integrated measurement. It exceeds the existing 8,000 guard. No guard was changed and no budget adoption was authorized by this evidence. Mesh counts are not measured GPU draw calls; array bytes are not actual device allocation or frame time.
+
+`docs/evidence/mira-head-v60/integration.patch` supplies four exact shared-module replacements: import the hair helper, apply NPC lid scale `[.0255,.019,.019]`, replace NPC brows and replace NPC hair. The actual `detailed-geometry.js` remains untouched. The test fixture applies those hooks in memory to the actual actor construction. Eyes, head/neck/lid bone names and eye centres `(±.046,.05,.109)` remain unchanged. The slightly larger lid repaired two exposed iris samples observed with the old lid and new face.
+
+The finite native checks passed:
+
+- Three dedicated candidate tests: original-source/provenance/closed face, shared geometry with independent skeletons, and monotonic sampled blink.
+- Seven existing UV/skin tests: original OBJ vertex/UV pairs and winding retained; production skin loader, ownership and smith-only assignment preserved.
+- Before/after isolated module graphs: all geometry attributes, indices, selected material properties, skeleton/rest and posed signatures identical for 13 other roles and four soldier themes.
+- Actual NPC neck rim: 46 vertices in five poses, zero points outside the existing neck ellipsoid; maximum normalized squared radius 0.662451. This checks the existing neck, not the new clothing author's collar surfaces.
+- Both eyes reached first by actual visible indexed triangles using double-sided rays at yaw −25°, 0°, +25°. The old full eight-step blink test also passes with the four hooks. These six central rays do not prove all camera views or all eyelid surface points.
+
+Indexed face slices make the authored change explicit: at head-local y=−.070 m the full width increases 157.415→173.469 mm; at y=.025 m the forward silhouette moves +4.584 mm. These slices include all head surfaces at that height (including ears where present), and are not labelled anatomical landmark distances. Hair maximum y=.203701 m exceeds the new face maximum y=.192504 m by 11.197 mm. Dialogue framing uses the face bounds; integrated hair framing still needs an actual comparison.
+
+The unchanged legacy tests were also preserved as honest failing evidence. Without the four assembly hooks, the old head suites have 3 pass / 5 fail: two old 1,646-triangle assertions, old morph provenance, old protected-shape coordinates, and the old lid. With the hooks, the anatomical suite has 4 pass / 1 fail, solely its old 1,646-triangle assertion. Those are not full-production acceptance. The old design assertions require deliberate integration updates if this design is adopted; this unit does not weaken them or the global triangle guard.
+
+The existing `young-male-q95.webp` was inspected as an original source image. Its visible stubble, baked eyelid/lip appearance and red mouth islands may conflict with the fixed Mira design. It is an existing CC0 graphical skin atlas, not a scan or proof of matching identity. The already shared 2048 atlas would not require a second image allocation for an extra material assignment, but that assignment remains **unadopted**. `src/skin-materials.js` is byte-identical to the baseline; the discarded opt-in implementation is retained only as `skin-candidate-review.patch`, explicitly not a production API or approved patch.
+
+The parent reported `GL_DISABLED`. This author did not invoke a browser, renderer, preview, alternate server or produce proxy screen images. Actual rendered likeness, light/material response, cloth/head intersections, mobile GPU performance, iPhone SE3 and whole-screen PS4 quality remain unverified. This is a saved candidate and a method-change boundary, not completion of the character or the 2026-09-20 quality objective.
+
+Reproduction: `node --test tests/mira-head-v60.test.mjs`; `node docs/evidence/mira-head-v60/measure.mjs` writes only `artifacts/mira-head-v60-measure.json`. The frozen old NPC data and shared-module hash manifest avoid dependency on another checkout or an unavailable historical commit. Generator default outputs go to `artifacts/mira-head-v60`; compare those outputs before copying them into runtime. No package/receipt/deployment was generated for this unadopted candidate.
+
+Timing: source implementation began 11:24:35 UTC; the first self-contained geometry checkpoint was saved before the 11:39:43 readback. Final generator replay took 20.507 seconds. The finite verification/recording boundary closed after the user's micro-part correction; exact close time and source hashes are in the evidence manifest. Tests are CPU/Node checks, not measured authoring time for each future micro-part.
